  {
    "name": "eligian_compile",
    "description": "Compile an Eligian (.eligian) program and inspect the Eligius JSON config it produces, with the Eligian map back to the source. `view`: `summary` (default without `select`: timelines with their source names, durations and action counts, the named / event action names, the operation counts, the controllers, the JSON size), `fragment` (default with `select`: one timeline by name, one named or event action by name, or the innermost action around a source `line`; no ids, each action with its `source` file / line / column) or `full` (the whole config, ids kept). `includeMap: true` adds the Eligian map entries of the returned actions (each operation with its source location). A program with errors returns `ok: false` and the same error diagnostics as `eligian_check`; a library file returns `ok: false, library: true`. `response_format: 'detailed'` adds the config's `cssFiles` and `languages` to the summary. `explain: true` adds, per returned operation, its JSON `path` and `origin` (the construct that generated it: source, call, target, erased-save, …) and, once per origin, the rule with the `eligian_docs` id to read; with `summary` only the operation counts per origin.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "path": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "select": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "timeline": {
              "type": "string"
            },
