  {
    "name": "eligian_project",
    "description": "The project inventory of an Eligian program: the css classes and ids, layout ids and classes, the selectors it may use, locales (languages, keys), host names, assets problems, files, outline and STORYBOARD.md counts. `path` is an entry .eligian file or a directory (every program under it gets a section; library files are listed under `files`). Read it before writing selectors or labels: `selectors` is what a selector may name (the CSS plus the layout HTML), `locales.keys` what a label may name. The `outline` lists the timelines (container, provider, `from`, compiled duration) with their events at resolved times, the actions with the role of each parameter, event actions, constants and named imports. `assets.problems` names missing media and named-import files, media timelines sharing one file and timeline containers missing from the layout. `storyboard` compares the beat rows of STORYBOARD.md per timeline with the compiled ranged timeline actions (`null` counts when the program does not compile). `response_format: 'detailed'` adds file sizes, the languages of each locale key and the starters. Nothing is written.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "path": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "response_format": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
